     2| * IVX Owner Conversation State — durable pending-action memory for owner-ai chat.
     3| *
     4| * Purpose: fix the conversation state-loss bug where the owner asks a question
     5| * ("How many properties do we have?"), the AI asks for permission, the owner
     6| * approves, and then the AI loses the original request and produces a generic
     7| * deployment plan.
     8| *
     9| * This service stores a structured pending-action record per conversation and
    10| * per owner. It is read/written on every owner-ai turn so follow-ups resolve
    11| * the original intent instead of being reinterpreted.
    12| *
    13| * Persistence: uses the same durable-store abstraction as ivx-ia-memory-store
    14| * (Supabase-backed when configured, otherwise local JSON). Survives Render
    15| * restarts and app reloads.
    16| *
    17| * Security: NEVER stores secrets, raw SQL, or credentials. Only stores the
    18| * owner-visible intent, target table/resource, and last-known status.
    19| */
    20|import { mkdir, readFile, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
    21|import path from 'node:path';
    22|import { auditDir } from './ivx-data-root';
    23|import {
    24|  isDurableStoreConfigured,
    25|  readDurableJson,
    26|  writeDurableJson,
    27|  appendDurableEvent,
    28|} from './ivx-durable-store';
